<title>NIGERIA: Nigeria's weekly forex demand rises to $95.4 mln.</title>
<headline>Nigeria's weekly forex demand rises to $95.4 mln.</headline>
<dateline>LAGOS 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nigeria's Central Bank said on Friday it sold $95.417 million naira at a rate of 80 to the dollar at its weekly auction this week.</p>
<p>Last week the bank sold $86.262 million naira at the same rate.</p>
<p>Demand for foreign exchange at the auction has risen steadily since mid-January when the government released its fiscal 1997 budget.</p>
<p>Bankers attributed the demand to rising economic activities.</p>
<p>--Lagos newsroom +234 1 263 03 17</p>
